=== layout: section

# Chapter 15: Plants and cell labeling

=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 24: Agrobacterium

@body

- Agrobacterium transfers DNA into plants. Molecular biologists borrowed the delivery system.
- Plant wound signals can activate bacterial virulence functions that help transfer *T-DNA*.
- Engineered vectors keep the transfer machinery while replacing tumor-causing functions with useful cargo.
- Transferring DNA, integrating it, and regenerating a plant are separate steps.

@notes

