=== layout: two-panels

# 24. Introducing genes into plants

@left

## Agrobacterium

- Transfer engineered T-DNA into plant cells.
- Ti-plasmid-based systems in culture
- Floral dip in suitable species

@right

## Particle bombardment

- Deliver DNA on small particles.
- Often uses gold particles
- Accelerated into plant tissue

@notes

Source: ../old/lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 66.
Converted layout or wording reviewed against the original slide. Original text and import diagnostics are retained in the review evidence.
2026 topic 24: Agrobacterium. Original content retained and regrouped.

=== layout: four-panels

# 24. Deliver, select, regenerate, check

@top-left

## Deliver

T-DNA border sequences define the transferred region. Vir proteins support the transfer.

@top-right

## Select

A selectable marker helps recover transformed cells. Selection does not prove every detail of the insertion.

@bottom-left

## Regenerate

Grow a plant from suitable tissue, or use a method such as floral dip in a suitable species.

@bottom-right

## Check

Confirm the insertion, expression, inheritance, and intended trait.

@notes

2026 topic 24; numbering authority: ../old/2026_topic_list.txt.
