=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 27: Monocultures

@body

- A field can be genetically uniform whether or not its crop was genetically engineered.
- Uniformity makes production predictable. It can also give a pathogen a lot of similar hosts.
- *Monoculture* describes a cropping system; *clonal propagation* describes reproduction.
- What matters is the diversity of resistance in the crop and the pathogen population around it.

@notes

