=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 28: GMO plants + nature

@body

- Nature keeps evolving after a crop is released.
- An engineered trait can move through reproduction with a compatible plant.
- Weeds and insects can also evolve resistance under repeated selection without acquiring a crop transgene.
- Gene flow and resistance evolution are related management problems, but they are different mechanisms.

@notes

