=== layout: two-panels

# 29. Count the bees. Then make the claim.

@left

## Adult hive experiment

- 600 bees per group returned to the hive.
- Fewer than 20% recaptured in each group.
- 15 per group assayed at each time point.

The paper does not report "9 survivors out of 45."

@right

## What can we conclude?

- Missing bees are not automatically dead bees.
- How could recapture bias the sample?
- Does mortality after Serratia challenge predict colony loss in the field?

@notes

Source: ../old/lect06c-set_4_TP-chapter_12-16_material.odp, slide 76.
2026 topic 29: glyphosate. Reconstructed from Motta, Raymann, and Moran (2018), including the supplementary methods, checked October 8, 2026.
https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1803880115
https://people.tamu.edu/~erick.motta/papers/motta2018pnas.pdf

Corrects the source's denominator: 45 is the assay sample across three groups at a time point, not the returned cohort. Recapture and survival are different endpoints.

