=== layout: one-panel

# Topic 30: Brainbow

@body

- How do you trace one neuron when it is tangled up with thousands of others?
- Brainbow gives neighboring cells different combinations of fluorescent proteins.
- *Cre recombinase* acts at compatible *lox* sites; the construct determines the possible DNA rearrangements.
- The resulting color helps follow a cell and its processes. It is a label, not a direct reading of what the neuron is thinking.

@notes

